-- §2  How often a claim says where it came from.
# One row per thing a claim says about its provenance, with how many claims say it.
#
# Almost nobody claims any standing
#   Three states, not two: a claim carrying provenance, a claim whose provenance was asked for and
#   refused, and a claim with no provenance element at all. Folding the last two would count a
#   silence as a refusal.
#
# This section is epistemics/standing.sqlc's reader
#   A relation nothing reads is a relation whose own header quotes a figure nobody recounts.
-- epistemics/standing.sqlc, folded to its three verdicts.
SELECT s.what_the_claim_says AS "says!", count(*) AS "claims!"
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/standing.sqlc)
) s
GROUP BY s.what_the_claim_says
ORDER BY count(*) DESC
